---
import AdSlot from "../../shared/AdSlot.astro";
import Layout from "../../shared/Layout.astro";
import SandboxFrame from "../../shared/SandboxFrame.astro";
import { toolJsonLd } from "../../shared/seo";
import { toolBySlug } from "../../tools/registry";

const tool = toolBySlug("csv-precheck");
const source = "https://github.com/xixiaofinland/salesforce-tools/blob/main";
---

<Layout
  title={`${tool.name}: Check Your CSV Before Import`}
  description={tool.description}
  jsonLd={toolJsonLd(tool, Astro.site!.href)}
>
  <h1>{tool.name}</h1>
  <p>
    Open a CSV file to check it. The file is opened in your browser and never leaves your computer.
    Don't take our word for it: disconnect from the internet and try again, it still works.
  </p>
  <SandboxFrame tool={tool.slug} title={tool.name} />
  <AdSlot name="csv-precheck-below-tool" />

  <!-- Every claim about Data Loader here comes from docs/research/data-loader-csv-facts.md. -->
  <section class="content">
    <h2>What it checks</h2>
    <p>
      The same rules Data Loader's own CSV reader applies. Each finding in the report explains
      itself.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>File:</strong> UTF-8 encoding, delimiter, size against Bulk API limits.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Header:</strong> missing, empty or duplicate column names.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rows:</strong> unclosed quotes, wrong column counts, stray spaces, duplicate rows.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>IDs:</strong> 15 or 18 characters, valid checksum, missing record IDs.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Dates:</strong> formats Data Loader accepts, day/month order, impossible dates.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Keys:</strong> values repeated in a column you pick, such as an external ID.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It can also convert 15-character IDs to 18, and split a large file into smaller ones as a zip.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Loader errors it helps prevent</h2>
    <p>Data Loader's own messages for the problems above.</p>
    <ul class="errors">
      <li>
        <code>
          CSV Error: Invalid CSV file format. Please select a different file. Error getting header
          row from the CSV file
        </code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>Error getting header row from the CSV file.</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>An empty column is found in the header row</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>A duplicate column [Name] is found</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>EOF reached before closing an opened quote</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>
          Error reading data row #2: the number of columns (5) exceeds the number of columns in the
          header (4)
        </code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>
          Error reading data row #1: the number of columns (3) is less than the number of columns in
          the header (4)
        </code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>MALFORMED_ID: Object name id: id value of incorrect type</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>MALFORMED_ID: bad id</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>MISSING_ARGUMENT: Id not specified in an update call</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>Error converting value to correct data type: Failed to parse date: 2024-02-30</code>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A row with the wrong column count stops the whole load; the report lists every such row at
      once.
    </p>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <h3>Is my file uploaded?</h3>
    <p>
      No. It is read in your browser, in a sandboxed frame that blocks every network request. Try it
      offline: it still works. The code is open source: see the
      <a href={`${source}/src/pages/sandbox/csv-precheck.astro`}>tool's page</a> and its
      <a href={`${source}/src/shared/sandbox/csp.ts`}>security policy</a> on GitHub.
    </p>
    <h3>Does it change my file?</h3>
    <p>
      No. Splitting and ID conversion give you new files; the converted copy differs only in its
      IDs.
    </p>
    <h3>Why is Data Loader's row number one less than the report's?</h3>
    <p>
      Data Loader counts from 0 and skips blank lines. The report counts from 1 and also gives the
      file's line number.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .content {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  /* Data Loader's messages are long and must not widen the page on a phone. */
  .errors code {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
